 "transcript": "Why does a photo get blurry when you zoom in? It's usually a raster image. A fixed grid of tiny colored squares called pixels. Zoom in and each pixel just gets bigger, so edges turn into steps. Many apps smooth those blocks, which looks blurry. A vector logo stores shapes as points and curves, so it's redrawn sharply at any size. Zooming can't add detail a photo never captured. Follow TensorBlue for software explained simply.",
